module j3.sys — Process / OS. Numbers are linux amd64; the Windows and macOS layers take the same `O_*` flags and map them (`openMode`).

fn: write open openMode read close lseek mmapAnon munmap onExit monotonicMs exit fork execve environ
    env setenv pipe dup2 chdir ioctl setsid canExec statAt lstatAt dirents rename unlink mkdir
    waitpid exitCode kill getpid pollFds ignoreSigpipe errno dlopen dlsym setThreadName panic
    panicAt argCount arg start exeDir fsync flock rmdir cwd pidfdOpen realpathTo
const: AT_FDCWD PLATFORM PLATFORM_LINUX PLATFORM_WINDOWS PLATFORM_MACOS PLATFORM_ANDROID
    PLATFORM_WEB PLATFORM_NAME ARCH ARCH_X86_64 ARCH_AARCH64 ARCH_X86 ARCH_ARM ARCH_RISCV ARCH_OTHER
    ARCH_NAME O_RDONLY O_WRONLY O_CREAT O_TRUNC SEEK_SET SEEK_END O_CLOEXEC WNOHANG SIGTERM SIGKILL
    O_RDWR O_NOCTTY SIGHUP POLLIN POLLOUT POLLERR POLLHUP O_EXCL LOCK_SH LOCK_EX LOCK_NB LOCK_UN
    EINTR EEXIST EWOULDBLOCK

signatures and comments: `j3c doc j3.sys`; one name: `j3c doc j3.sys <name>`
